    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110762" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φθόρ-φῐ</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φθόρ-φῐν</span></b> , case-suffix with locative, ablative and
		instrumental sense, freq. in 
			Ep.
		; also 
			Aeol.
		 acc. to Sch.D, Gen.<i><span class="en">
			Il.
			3.338
		</span></i>, Sch. <i><span class="en">
			Opp.
			<u>Hal.</u>
			1.709
		</span></i>; 
			Boeot.
		 acc. to <i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πασσαλόφιν</span>
			 (who cites <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἴδηφιν</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἴδης</span>
			); found in Lyr., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σὺν ὄχεσφι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ibyc.
					2.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μῶσα . . , ὠρανίαφι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alcm.
					59
				</span></i>
			 (voc. acc. to <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Adv.</u>
				165.8
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πασσαλόφιν</span> in a Com.
			parody, <i><span class="en">
				Hermipp.
				55
			</span></i> (anap.).</div>
